                <pb facs="0526" n="454" xml:id="pg454"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 6369/272.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Merry to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">San
                            Jose</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1909-11-15"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">November 15,
                    1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Merry acknowledges department’s telegram of 12th, and says President of Costa
                    Rica promises adherence to the Washington conventions, and states that
                    Nicaraguan Government has apologized for invasion.</p>
            </div>
